Successful deployments depend on thorough preparation. A deployment checklist ensures that every prerequisite has been verified before resources are provisioned in Azure.

The checklist should include:

* Subscription validation
* Resource group creation
* Naming convention verification
* RBAC assignments
* Network configuration
* Security policies
* Backup planning
* Monitoring setup
* Cost estimation
* Documentation updates

For example, before deploying a production application, administrators verify that monitoring alerts, backup policies, and network security groups are correctly configured.

A real-life use case is organizations reducing deployment failures by standardizing implementation procedures across multiple teams.

Deployment planning minimizes errors and improves operational consistency.
